      "summaries": {
        "en": "pi-subagents extends the Pi framework to enable asynchronous delegation of tasks to sub-agents, solving the problem of managing complex, multi-step workflows. Its key technical insight is supporting truncation, artifacts, and session sharing, allowing sub-agents to pass intermediate results and maintain context efficiently. You can use it to build modular AI systems where a primary agent orchestrates specialized sub-agents for subtasks like data retrieval or code generation, improving scalability and maintainability.",
        "zh": "pi-subagents 是 Pi 框架的扩展，用于实现异步子代理任务委派，解决复杂多步骤工作流的管理难题。其核心技术亮点是支持截断、工件和会话共享，使子代理能高效传递中间结果并保持上下文连贯。你可以用它构建模块化 AI 系统：主代理将数据检索、代码生成等子任务分派给专用子代理，从而提升系统的可扩展性和可维护性。",
        "es": "pi-subagents extends the Pi framework to enable asynchronous delegation of tasks to sub-agents, solving the problem of managing complex, multi-step workflows. Its key technical insight is supporting truncation, artifacts, and session sharing, allowing sub-agents to pass intermediate results and maintain context efficiently. You can use it to build modular AI systems where a primary agent orchestrates specialized sub-agents for subtasks like data retrieval or code generation, improving scalability and maintainability.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "pi-subagents gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "pi-subagents extends the Pi framework to enable asynchronous delegation of tasks to sub-agents, solving the problem of managing complex, multi-step workflows. Its key technical insight is supporting truncation, artifacts, and session sharing, allowing sub-agents to pass intermediate results and maintain context efficiently. You can use it to build modular AI systems where a primary agent orchestrates specialized sub-agents for subtasks like data retrieval or code generation, improving scalability and maintainability.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/nicobailon/pi-subagents for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
