      "summaries": {
        "en": "Kimi-K2.6 is a multimodal model that processes both images and text for conversational AI, aiming to deliver accurate visual understanding alongside dialogue. Technically, it uses compressed tensors and a custom architecture derived from the Kimi K2.5 series, enabling efficient feature extraction from visual inputs. You can deploy it for tasks like image captioning, visual question answering, or interactive chatbots that discuss photos. Experiment with it via Hugging Face Transformers for research or prototyping.",
        "zh": "Kimi-K2.6 是一个多模态模型，能同时处理图像和文本，用于对话式 AI，目标是实现精准的视觉理解与自然对话的结合。技术上，它采用压缩张量和基于 Kimi K2.5 系列的自定义架构，能从视觉输入中高效提取特征。你可以用它做图像描述、视觉问答或能讨论照片的交互式聊天机器人。通过 Hugging Face Transformers 即可部署，适合研究或原型开发。",
        "es": "Kimi-K2.6 is a multimodal model that processes both images and text for conversational AI, aiming to deliver accurate visual understanding alongside dialogue. Technically, it uses compressed tensors and a custom architecture derived from the Kimi K2.5 series, enabling efficient feature extraction from visual inputs. You can deploy it for tasks like image captioning, visual question answering, or interactive chatbots that discuss photos. Experiment with it via Hugging Face Transformers for research or prototyping.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Kimi-K2.6 stands out for transformers, safetensors, and kimi_k25 in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Kimi-K2.6 is a multimodal model that processes both images and text for conversational AI, aiming to deliver accurate visual understanding alongside dialogue. Technically, it uses compressed tensors and a custom architecture derived from the Kimi K2.5 series, enabling efficient feature extraction from visual inputs. You can deploy it for tasks like image captioning, visual question answering, or interactive chatbots that discuss photos. Experiment with it via Hugging Face Transformers for research or prototyping.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
